**The main risk is that “an unargued view” can be read more broadly than the standard’s rejection of a *general* view.** For example, a named analyst’s new, specific judgment could affect an investment question even if the article does not give its reasoning.

I audited only [review-core-v60.txt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/review-core-v60.txt) against version 4 of the [extraction standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:356). I did not assess questions, fields or matching. As requested, I do not count the loss of §6’s optional items as a breach.

The Chinese quotations below are exact. An English example can be a faithful translation or adaptation of a standard example without being the same literal text; I identify those separately.

## Clause-by-clause audit

| Text under audit | Standard line | Classification and reason |
|---|---|---|
| “Before you return the answer, check it once.” | §5.1: “从第一段读到最后一段，分析员会记的都留。” | **CONSISTENT.** The final check serves the standard’s instruction to retain everything the analyst would note. |
| “Read each evidence item back as the analyst following the company and keep it when you would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely” | §5.1: “一个在追这家公司的分析员，读到会在本周笔记里写下来，因为它让某个问题的答案更可能或更不可能。” | **CONSISTENT.** This carries the standard’s central test. |
| “about the company or its customers, suppliers, competitors, regulators or the economy.” | §5.1: “问题不限于库里已有的，也不限于本公司：客户、供应商、竞争者、监管、宏观都算” | **CONSISTENT.** The scope matches this line, though §5.1’s four kinds also explicitly mention partners. |
| “Ask first whether it is new” | §5.1: “判一句话之前先问：这是新信息吗？” | **CONSISTENT.** It follows the standard’s first question. |
| “repeated common knowledge” | §5.1: “重复常识……是杂音” | **CONSISTENT.** This matches the standard’s noise category. |
| “a long-standing situation retold” | §5.1: “描述长期状况……是杂音”; §5.3: “看不出是旧事的不算重提” | **CONSISTENT.** The qualification “retold,” read with the later boundary, avoids treating every newly reported long-standing condition as a repeat. |
| “an unargued view” | §5.1: “泛泛的看法，是杂音” and “一个新的具体判断，是增量，不能漏”; §5.3: “作者的一般性风险清单和没有推导的看法” | **WIDER-DROP.** “Unargued” can include a new, specific judgment even though the standard protects such judgments when the analyst would note them. |
| “guidance, and a forecast or a plan still in force, keep their place even when retold.” | §5.3: “重提的季度指引和仍然有效的预测、计划按本来分量” | **CONSISTENT.** It carries the required exception for retold guidance and still-effective forecasts and plans. |
| “These usually fail that check:” | §5.2: “下面的不留清单不能用来删掉分析员会记的陈述”; §6: “先看那一行的‘边界’一列” | **CONSISTENT.** “Usually” makes the listed classes subordinate to the check, although the boundaries still need to be clear. |
| “background the analyst already knew: an arrangement already in place, described again; the company's history” | §5.1: “常识，就是跟这家公司的分析员读这篇之前就已经知道的” and “对已知状况的重述”; §5.3: “记者的背景和框架” | **CONSISTENT.** These are descriptions of known background, subject to the retelling boundary. |
| “A development the item reports without making clear that it is old is not a retelling” | §5.3: “文字或日期看不出是旧事的不算重提” | **CONSISTENT.** This carries the D243 item 6 boundary. |
