| “a typical claim that is common knowledge, without a figure and a specific account: that a firm leads or competes, that demand is strong or supply tight, a general risk” | §5.1: “谁领先、谁在竞争、需求强、供给紧……这类说法” and “这类陈述没有数字和具体的叙事就不收”; §5.3: “作者的一般性风险清单” | **CONSISTENT.** The wording limits this rejection to common knowledge and general risk. |
| “a figure alone does not lift it” | §5.1: “有数字也要过上面的规则” | **CONSISTENT.** A number alone does not replace the analyst’s judgment. |
| “a product, game, driver or benchmark detail with no business scale” | §5.3: “没有业务规模的产品、游戏、驱动、跑分细节” | **CONSISTENT.** The class matches, with the standard’s exceptions assessed below. |
