| “the product line launched in 2020” | §5.3: “A100 2020 年上市” | **CONSISTENT.** A generalized adaptation of the page example; general, though its historical-background context matters. |
| “that a firm leads or competes” | §5.1: “谁领先、谁在竞争” | **CONSISTENT.** A translation of the page’s common-knowledge examples; general. |
| “that demand is strong or supply tight” | §5.1: “需求强、供给紧” | **CONSISTENT.** A translation of the page’s examples; general. |
| “if demand slows it would hurt” | §5.3: “如果 AI 退潮会受伤” | **CONSISTENT.** A generalized adaptation of the page’s empty-risk example; general. |
| “the leading soft-drink brand has held 40% of its market for years”, in an article about a bank | §5.1: “作者说‘英特尔多年领先，占 CPU 市场 59%’，和英伟达的问题关系不大，分析员不会记。” | **CONSISTENT.** The principle follows the page’s irrelevant longstanding-figure example, but the soft-drink figure and bank scenario are **invented**, not examples from the page; the scenario is bank-specific, even though the irrelevance principle is general. |
| “the card draws 415 watts” | §5.3: “这张卡 415W” | **CONSISTENT.** A direct translation of the page example; it is a hardware example, so it does not itself read as an example for every industry. |
